\label{lem:amalgamation}
Suppose that $p$ and $q$ are separated twins and that $D_p\ne\varnothing$.
Let $x=\min D_p$.  For each $i<2$ there is a good precondition
$r\leq p,q$ such that
\begin{displaymath}
 h^r(\{x,\sigma(x)\})=i.
\end{displaymath}
